            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with increasing pain after cholecystectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8720</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 25-year-old female presented with abdominal pain and collapse 3 days after a laparoscopic cholecystectomy. The MRCP images suggested a leakage from the stump of the cystic duct. However, an ERCP showed a leakage of a subvesical bile duct arriving from the left hepatic duct. Diagnostic and treatment modalities are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
